WEBVTT

00:06.310 --> 00:08.320
Witch: Nishimura

00:14.030 --> 00:18.530
Prince: Hashimoto
Princess: Watanabe
Witch: Nishimura

00:14.190 --> 00:18.150
<i>I didn't expect this to happen 
during my short absence...</i>

00:18.530 --> 00:21.000
Is your stomach feeling better now?

00:21.000 --> 00:21.860
Yeah!

00:21.860 --> 00:24.970
Three cartons of milk from lunch
was apparently too much for me.

00:24.970 --> 00:27.950
Now, why are you playing
 the witch, Nishimura-san?

00:27.950 --> 00:30.300
"Why not?" "She's creepy." "It fits her."

00:30.300 --> 00:32.700
Probably something along those lines.

00:38.600 --> 00:41.680
A witch... A witch, huh?

00:41.680 --> 00:43.140
Wh-What's wrong with that?

00:43.140 --> 00:45.730
I think you're a little 
too cute to be a witch!

00:45.730 --> 00:46.730
What?

00:46.950 --> 00:49.200
C'mon, give me a break, Takada!

00:49.200 --> 00:50.830
We're talking about Nishimura!

00:50.830 --> 00:51.740
The Grim Reaper!

00:54.570 --> 00:58.450
None of you realize how 
scary real witches are.

00:58.810 --> 01:00.170
Huh?

00:59.390 --> 01:01.250
What are you talking about?

01:01.440 --> 01:05.630
Witches are supposed to be
super old and frightening.

01:05.630 --> 01:10.110
They brew weird potions 
and eat children from the village.

01:10.110 --> 01:14.330
So whoever's playing the witch needs
to be <i>really</i> scary.

01:14.630 --> 01:17.520
Not some cutie in a costume like this!

01:24.650 --> 01:26.530
A witch wearing a tank top...

01:26.900 --> 01:29.420
Y-You mean the costume is cute, right?

01:29.420 --> 01:33.390
The costume is to cutesy
for what you had in mind, right?

01:33.390 --> 01:36.380
It's not like I was trying to make it cute.

01:36.380 --> 01:38.920
I just used the scraps we had lying around.

01:38.920 --> 01:43.970
Oh, so it just looks cute
because Nishimura-san is wearing it.

01:44.520 --> 01:47.410
Everyone <i>did</i> say it would suit you!

01:51.390 --> 01:53.560
Isn't that great, Nishimura-san?

01:53.560 --> 01:54.970
Y-Yeah...

01:54.970 --> 01:57.960
But you're nowhere near
scary enough for the role,

01:57.960 --> 01:59.830
so you'll really have to act the part.

01:59.830 --> 02:02.770
As you are, you're way too cute!

02:02.770 --> 02:04.470
Y-Yeah, I get it...

02:04.470 --> 02:05.960
I get it already...

02:08.320 --> 02:09.930
<i>Autumn is here.</i>

02:09.930 --> 02:12.340
<i>There's so much to do in store for us.</i>

03:38.900 --> 03:42.990
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

03:43.780 --> 03:49.240
<i>Episode 8 "Yukata, Jungle Gyms, and Orthopedic Casts"</i>

03:44.100 --> 03:47.750
Eek, how cute!

03:47.750 --> 03:49.910
Um, Yukiko-san,

03:49.910 --> 03:53.260
are you sure it's okay for 
me to have this yukata?

03:54.150 --> 03:55.660
It's totally fine!

03:55.660 --> 03:57.710
It doesn't fit me anymore.

03:59.130 --> 04:02.280
Ah, so precious!

03:59.620 --> 04:02.830
But you gave me clothes last time, too...

04:03.550 --> 04:05.450
Seriously, don't worry about it.

04:05.450 --> 04:07.740
Just come to my school festival wearing this.

04:07.740 --> 04:09.020
Your school festival?

04:09.730 --> 04:10.520
That's right!

04:10.520 --> 04:12.060
You can come with Taiyou.

04:12.060 --> 04:13.050
What?!

04:13.050 --> 04:18.450
It's open to the public, and kids from the 
local elementary school check it out every year.

04:20.290 --> 04:21.560
What's the matter?

04:21.950 --> 04:23.070
It's nothing...

04:23.330 --> 04:24.890
<i>Is it really all right...</i>

04:24.890 --> 04:27.880
<i>for the Grim Reaper 
to wear such a cute yukata?</i>

04:28.200 --> 04:31.120
<i>What would Takada-kun think of it?</i>

04:32.580 --> 04:33.940
I'm back!

04:33.940 --> 04:35.900
I got the soy sauce you asked for!

04:36.200 --> 04:37.080
Huh?

04:37.770 --> 04:40.460
It's nothing like I imagined...

04:42.680 --> 04:44.350
What are you talking about?

04:44.350 --> 04:45.820
She looks totally great.

04:45.820 --> 04:49.030
Yeah! I think it looks good on her, too!

04:49.030 --> 04:49.680
Oh?

04:50.040 --> 04:52.240
That's why I was so surprised!

04:52.240 --> 04:54.440
You don't look like the Grim Reaper at all!

04:56.180 --> 05:00.140
You're just a normal cute 
girl today, Nishimura-san!

05:04.820 --> 05:08.020
That means you'll need to protect her.

05:08.020 --> 05:09.330
That's true!

05:09.330 --> 05:12.030
I need to protect Nishimura-san!

05:13.440 --> 05:16.170
You really are so straightforward.

05:16.170 --> 05:20.500
But for some reason, 
this makes me kind of nervous...

05:24.920 --> 05:27.430
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

05:27.420 --> 05:28.910
Welcome!

05:27.430 --> 05:30.680
<b>That-There Middle School Cultural Festival</b>

05:28.160 --> 05:30.670
Would you like to try our crepes?

05:36.820 --> 05:38.650
Wow, this is amazing!

05:38.650 --> 05:40.810
Everything looks so tasty!

05:43.270 --> 05:45.940
Thanks for visiting, you two!

05:45.940 --> 05:55.870
Café

05:46.120 --> 05:48.760
That's some outfit you have on.

05:48.760 --> 05:51.780
Well, it <i>is</i> the festival!

05:51.780 --> 05:55.880
At our school, 
we stake our lives on this event.

05:55.880 --> 05:57.290
Your lives?

05:57.290 --> 05:59.500
You're so cool, Onee-chan!

05:59.500 --> 06:02.040
You look pretty spiffy yourself.

06:02.040 --> 06:05.210
Make sure you do a good job 
escorting Nishimura-san.

06:05.210 --> 06:06.010
Yeah!

06:06.010 --> 06:09.300
Wait, you're not going to 
come with us, Yukiko-san?

06:09.610 --> 06:11.710
I've got to look after the shop!

06:12.250 --> 06:15.210
I <i>am</i> this café's beautiful poster girl!

06:18.780 --> 06:21.710
Takada, stop flattering yourself.

06:22.240 --> 06:24.740
Onee-chan, they've got your number!

06:24.740 --> 06:27.480
And so, I'm sorry I can't go with you.

06:27.480 --> 06:28.710
O-Oh, it's okay.

06:29.230 --> 06:31.350
<i>It'll just be the two of us.</i>

06:35.780 --> 06:37.410
<i>That...</i>

06:41.710 --> 06:44.670
Haunted House

06:41.940 --> 06:43.160
<i>almost...</i>

06:44.660 --> 06:47.010
<i>sounds like a date!</i>

06:48.130 --> 06:49.640
They're so cute!

06:49.640 --> 06:51.080
You're right!

06:51.080 --> 06:53.550
The school festival's so much fun!

06:54.090 --> 06:57.640
Yukiko-san gave us so many 
tickets for these booths.

06:57.640 --> 07:00.060
We should thank her later.

07:00.590 --> 07:01.530
Hey, hey!

07:01.530 --> 07:03.060
Where should we go next?

07:03.060 --> 07:13.030
<b>Yakisoba</b>

07:03.260 --> 07:05.380
Crepes? Choco bananas?

07:05.380 --> 07:06.160
Huh?

07:06.160 --> 07:08.610
L-Let's take a break for now.

07:08.610 --> 07:10.890
We can get candied apples for dessert!

07:10.890 --> 07:12.450
O-Okay...

07:13.030 --> 07:16.470
M-Middle school really is amazing.

07:16.470 --> 07:18.520
Everyone seems so grown up.

07:18.520 --> 07:19.210
Huh?

07:19.840 --> 07:22.260
Do you think we will, too?

07:22.580 --> 07:25.210
<b>Takoyaki</b>

07:22.590 --> 07:24.120
Just like them?

07:25.200 --> 07:26.600
You mean grow up?

07:27.030 --> 07:28.730
Oh, yeah.

07:30.520 --> 07:32.140
Nishimura-san?

07:32.920 --> 07:35.940
I'm not sure why...

07:35.940 --> 07:41.010
But thinking about the future
makes me a little sad.

07:44.350 --> 07:45.790
Ah, I'm sorry!

07:45.790 --> 07:47.490
We should be having fun.

07:47.490 --> 07:49.490
No, I get it.

07:49.490 --> 07:53.990
Things are so much fun right now, 
which just makes it sadder.

07:55.090 --> 07:56.510
<i>I see now.</i>

07:56.510 --> 08:01.490
<i>I'm having fun now
that I don't want it to end.</i>

08:01.490 --> 08:04.210
But I'll do something about it!

08:04.210 --> 08:06.740
So you don't have any time to feel sad!

08:06.930 --> 08:10.100
I'll do everything I can
to make you smile every day!

08:12.260 --> 08:14.500
As thanks for always hanging out with me!

08:15.100 --> 08:19.110
O-Oh, no, I should be the one thanking...

08:19.880 --> 08:20.810
Hmm?

08:22.020 --> 08:27.520
<b>That-There Middle School Cultural Festival</b>

08:22.220 --> 08:25.410
F-For some reason, I don't feel sad anymore.

08:25.410 --> 08:26.730
That was quick!

08:30.530 --> 08:32.530
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

08:33.430 --> 08:35.530
I saw you, Takada!

08:37.530 --> 08:40.500
You went on a date with 
the Grim Reaper, right?

08:40.900 --> 08:42.440
A date?

08:42.440 --> 08:46.150
You were hanging out with the 
Grim Reaper in yukata!

08:46.150 --> 08:47.920
At the middle school.

08:47.920 --> 08:49.220
Oh!

08:50.030 --> 08:52.910
Yukatamura-san was so cute!

08:52.910 --> 08:55.370
Nobody cares about that!

08:55.370 --> 08:57.770
You two were on a date!

08:58.580 --> 09:00.830
We were just hanging out.

09:01.550 --> 09:04.510
That was so obviously a date!

09:05.390 --> 09:06.950
Really?

09:06.950 --> 09:11.350
I've never been on a date before, 
so I'm glad my first was with Nishimura-san!

09:11.710 --> 09:13.680
I didn't ask...

09:13.680 --> 09:15.310
That's a hard pass from me.

09:15.310 --> 09:17.700
Who wants to go on a date 
with the Grim Reaper?

09:17.700 --> 09:19.330
Wait, what?!

09:19.330 --> 09:21.200
We're talking about a god!

09:21.400 --> 09:24.430
A god? Yeah, the god of <i>death</i>!

09:24.430 --> 09:26.700
Still a god.

09:26.980 --> 09:28.680
So you wouldn't mind

09:28.680 --> 09:32.720
if I spread it through the school
that you two went on a date?

09:32.720 --> 09:35.720
I'm sure everyone will tease you to death.

09:35.720 --> 09:38.720
What?! That's, well...

09:38.930 --> 09:39.980
Figures.

09:39.980 --> 09:42.880
That'd be embarrassing even for you.

09:42.880 --> 09:45.510
Yeah, it'd be like bragging.

09:46.810 --> 09:48.490
My butt, it would!

09:54.230 --> 09:56.950
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

09:58.710 --> 10:04.250
<i>The days grew shorter and shorter 
as our fall field day drew closer.</i>

10:05.330 --> 10:14.800
<b>That-There Elementary School
Field Day Guide</b>

10:05.330 --> 10:14.800
Venue: That-There Elementary School Campus

10:05.760 --> 10:08.020
Oh, wow!

10:08.020 --> 10:11.280
There'll be five teams for field day here.

10:11.280 --> 10:14.790
Back at my old school, we only 
had a red team and a white team!

10:15.010 --> 10:16.510
I can't wait!

10:16.510 --> 10:19.880
Footraces, the ball toss, 
rolling a giant ball...

10:19.880 --> 10:22.280
You can leave the bread-eating contest to me!

10:23.100 --> 10:24.730
Y-Yeah...

10:26.080 --> 10:27.600
What's the matter?

10:27.600 --> 10:30.760
Huh? Wh-What do you mean?

10:31.210 --> 10:32.980
You don't look very excited.

10:33.350 --> 10:37.650
Could it be that you don't like field days?

10:39.640 --> 10:41.480
Well...

10:41.730 --> 10:44.500
Field day is just around the corner.

10:44.720 --> 10:47.450
I sure hope we don't lose!

10:47.450 --> 10:50.250
Thanks to the Grim Reaper's curse, that is.

10:52.200 --> 10:56.220
Does the power of your curse mean 
that we can't win field day?

10:56.630 --> 10:58.310
They're just saying what they want.

10:58.730 --> 11:02.580
Apparently, the Grim Reaper's team never wins.

11:04.000 --> 11:04.850
Oh!

11:05.390 --> 11:09.570
So you can't control the 
power of your mighty curse!

11:11.340 --> 11:13.510
That's not it at all.

11:14.760 --> 11:16.570
That sure is awesome!

11:16.570 --> 11:21.360
You're not even trying to use your curse, 
yet it affects who wins!

11:21.360 --> 11:24.700
I-It's nothing that impressive.

11:25.120 --> 11:26.000
Huh?

11:26.000 --> 11:31.880
But if the Grim Reaper's team is destined 
to lose, what happens if you win?

11:33.640 --> 11:35.440
What do you mean?

11:35.440 --> 11:38.510
If the team cursed to always 
lose ends up winning,

11:38.510 --> 11:43.140
would that mean that your 
curse is a bunch of baloney?

11:45.160 --> 11:47.930
If that's the case...

11:48.850 --> 11:51.440
What do we do if we win?

11:51.440 --> 11:53.430
I-It's fine.

11:53.430 --> 11:55.700
Just be happy if that happens!

11:58.740 --> 12:02.210
Y-You're a really fast runner, Takada-kun.

12:02.210 --> 12:04.810
This is your chance to shine!

12:04.810 --> 12:10.110
But if I win, it'll mean
your powers aren't real...

12:10.450 --> 12:13.620
That's just something they made up!

12:13.620 --> 12:17.190
So don't you worry about me.

12:19.210 --> 12:20.560
Okay!

12:20.560 --> 12:21.940
In that case, I'll win!

12:22.690 --> 12:25.080
You can leave field day to me!

12:25.890 --> 12:27.520
S-Sure...

12:28.600 --> 12:35.520
Turns out my 50-meter dash is far and
away the best time in the entire school!

12:35.760 --> 12:37.460
Th-That's incredible.

12:38.270 --> 12:40.570
I heard it from our teacher the other day!

12:40.570 --> 12:42.280
Do your best, then.

12:42.280 --> 12:44.500
In my place...

12:46.860 --> 12:48.250
In your place?

12:48.520 --> 12:54.520
I'm really slow, and I'm sure I won't 
be of any use for our class...

12:55.920 --> 13:00.860
Hey, Nishimura-san,
have you ever climbed up to the top?

13:03.040 --> 13:05.260
N-No, I haven't.

13:07.760 --> 13:09.450
Try climbing it!

13:09.450 --> 13:10.210
Huh?

13:12.860 --> 13:15.230
No way. I can't do that.

13:15.440 --> 13:18.480
It's fine! I'll give you a hand!

13:34.490 --> 13:36.530
I-It's so windy!

13:36.750 --> 13:39.540
Just relax. I've got you.

14:05.030 --> 14:06.120
Are you okay?

14:06.120 --> 14:08.100
There's not much footing, so watch out.

14:08.500 --> 14:09.890
O-Okay.

14:10.520 --> 14:12.830
The view's great up here!

14:12.830 --> 14:15.040
You can see real far out!

14:16.490 --> 14:18.590
I-It's beautiful.

14:18.840 --> 14:21.090
Hey, that's the sea over there!

14:22.490 --> 14:27.920
It's been a while since I moved here, 
but there's still so much I don't know.

14:29.330 --> 14:32.180
Like the fact that there are 
five colors of teams for field day!

14:33.110 --> 14:35.360
Just like a squad of heroes!

14:37.440 --> 14:38.600
I guess you're right.

14:38.970 --> 14:43.070
I'm sure you'll make plenty of new 
discoveries from here on out, too.

14:43.490 --> 14:45.500
But you know, Nishimura-san...

14:45.500 --> 14:48.570
I want to share all of that with you.

14:48.570 --> 14:49.430
Huh?

14:50.850 --> 14:55.830
Rather than be alone,
I'll do my best to stick with you.

14:58.190 --> 14:59.280
Hey!

14:59.280 --> 15:01.390
What are you two doing?

15:01.390 --> 15:03.630
Let's hurry up and go home!

15:04.870 --> 15:08.300
Those two are in the heyday of their youth.

15:08.300 --> 15:10.690
What does "heyday" mean?

15:11.600 --> 15:18.450
<i>I also want to be with Takada-kun 
instead of having him take my place...</i>

15:20.280 --> 15:22.100
T-Takada-kun.

15:22.890 --> 15:24.180
I also...

15:31.100 --> 15:33.080
Ah! Nishimura-san!

15:46.900 --> 15:48.830
T-Takada-kun!

15:48.830 --> 15:50.210
Takada!

15:50.850 --> 15:54.170
That sounded really bad just now!

15:57.520 --> 15:58.990
Are you okay?!

15:59.510 --> 16:01.800
I-I'll go get a teacher!

16:01.800 --> 16:02.700
Thanks!

16:08.050 --> 16:08.870
Ah...

16:14.650 --> 16:19.130
<i>Instead of giving up my place,
 I also want to...</i>

16:21.370 --> 16:24.750
<b>That-There General Hospital</b>

16:37.760 --> 16:39.680
Nishimura Akane-chan?

16:46.270 --> 16:49.090
Hey there. I'm Taiyou's mother.

16:49.720 --> 16:50.480
Eh?

16:52.580 --> 16:53.720
Nice to meet you!

16:54.140 --> 16:55.830
I'm Akane's father.

16:55.830 --> 16:58.320
I'm so sorry for all the trouble...

16:58.570 --> 17:01.220
Um, is Takada-kun's arm...

17:01.790 --> 17:03.820
It snapped clean in two!

17:07.710 --> 17:08.860
Like a twig!

17:08.860 --> 17:10.950
But don't you worry.

17:10.950 --> 17:13.110
They're looking after it as we speak.

17:15.890 --> 17:18.670
I'm truly so sorry about this.

17:19.130 --> 17:20.170
Oh, no!

17:20.170 --> 17:23.390
It's my son's fault for horsing around.

17:23.390 --> 17:28.430
I'm just glad that Akane-chan 
isn't hurt any worse.

17:28.890 --> 17:30.590
B-But...

17:31.380 --> 17:34.750
Takada-kun got hurt trying to protect me!

17:34.750 --> 17:36.230
It's my fault!

17:37.130 --> 17:40.830
If I hadn't climbed up there with him...

17:41.500 --> 17:45.630
He was so excited about field day, too...

17:51.120 --> 17:57.340
I've done something
I can never, ever take back...

17:58.600 --> 18:00.090
I'm so sorry!

18:02.110 --> 18:03.270
Akane...

18:03.270 --> 18:04.460
How nice!

18:07.860 --> 18:10.940
It's so nice of you to apologize 
like that, Akane-chan!

18:11.610 --> 18:14.710
Thanks for crying on Taiyou's behalf.

18:18.290 --> 18:24.380
You know, Akane-chan, you can make up for
most of the small mistakes you make as a kid.

18:25.680 --> 18:30.050
Breaking a bone is a small mistake?

18:30.490 --> 18:31.710
Did you know?

18:31.710 --> 18:36.150
Bones heal faster when you're a kid
and when it's a clean break.

18:36.150 --> 18:39.840
Luckily, that's how it turned 
out this time, so it's fine.

18:39.840 --> 18:44.130
Winding up in a cast is something you
look back on and laugh about as a grown-up.

18:45.550 --> 18:46.840
As a grown-up...

18:48.060 --> 18:54.580
Besides, I'm sure Taiyou would say, 
"I'm glad you didn't get hurt!"

18:55.290 --> 18:57.440
Th-That can't be...

18:58.070 --> 19:00.320
Hey, I'm being serious here.

19:00.320 --> 19:03.360
My son just adores you!

19:07.000 --> 19:10.660
Ever since we moved here, 
you're all he talks about at home.

19:10.660 --> 19:13.620
How he's made a really wonderful friend.

19:14.700 --> 19:18.350
He says being with you just 
makes everything more fun!

19:25.640 --> 19:29.230
So you've got nothing to feel guilty about.

19:29.230 --> 19:32.150
He protected you because he wanted to.

19:35.070 --> 19:38.720
Thank you for playing with Taiyou 
all the time, Akane-chan.

19:40.070 --> 19:42.400
Please keep on being good 
friends with my son!

19:42.400 --> 19:45.890
Th-Thank you very much...

19:47.440 --> 19:50.000
Oh, I'm so sorry!

19:50.000 --> 19:52.160
Lecturing someone else's child like that...

19:52.510 --> 19:54.420
No, hardly.

19:54.910 --> 19:59.860
I feel like I understand better now where 
Taiyou-kun gets all his honesty from.

20:00.160 --> 20:02.780
We're just simple folks.

20:02.780 --> 20:04.920
Me and Taiyou both.

20:12.580 --> 20:15.430
I think Taiyou will be okay 
to go to school tomorrow.

20:23.020 --> 20:26.970
<i>If Takada-kun is feeling down tomorrow...</i>

20:28.040 --> 20:30.480
<i>I'll need to cheer him up!</i>

22:08.850 --> 22:11.440
Akane-chan, are you all right?

22:11.790 --> 22:14.080
Yeah, I'm fine.

22:14.080 --> 22:16.930
I'm more worried about Takada-kun.

22:16.930 --> 22:18.250
Nishimura-san!

22:18.510 --> 22:20.860
Nishimura-san!

22:21.440 --> 22:23.150
Check out my arm!

22:23.150 --> 22:25.730
It's like the Dark Dragon is sealed within!

22:25.730 --> 22:27.330
So cool!

22:28.250 --> 22:30.200
I know, right?

22:30.200 --> 22:31.600
<i>He's A-okay!</i>

22:32.430 --> 22:33.880
Are you going to be okay?

22:34.340 --> 22:36.640
No, far from it.

22:36.640 --> 22:41.200
Keeping the Dark Dragon sealed 
away is very mentally taxing...

22:41.200 --> 22:44.290
No, I meant f-field day.

22:44.290 --> 22:46.210
You can't participate anymore.

22:46.520 --> 22:48.920
Well, no point crying over spilled milk!

22:48.920 --> 22:51.220
We'll have field day next year, too.

22:51.400 --> 22:53.650
Also, my arm...

22:54.210 --> 22:59.340
It snapped really cleanly, so they said 
it might heal up before field day!

23:01.530 --> 23:03.510
R-Really?

23:03.940 --> 23:07.450
I've always wanted to wear a cast!

23:07.800 --> 23:09.200
Isn't it cool?

23:09.200 --> 23:11.100
It's heavier than it looks!

23:11.400 --> 23:12.690
I'm so relieved...

23:12.950 --> 23:15.410
I'm really so glad!

23:15.410 --> 23:16.440
I know!

23:16.960 --> 23:19.970
I'm glad you didn't get hurt!

23:21.450 --> 23:25.090
<i>He really said it, word for word.</i>

23:28.970 --> 23:31.450
Huh? Why did you laugh?

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next time...</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Run! Shout! Field Day</b>
